# {{ title }}

## Headings

Headings use `#` to `######` followed by a space. There is no underline style, so `---` is always a horizontal rule.

### Generated IDs

Every heading gets an ID from its text. This section's ID is `generated-ids`, so you can [link to it](#generated-ids).

### Explicit IDs {#stable-id}

Add `{#id}` at the end of a heading to fix its ID. Links to it keep working even if you rename the heading: [jump to the explicit ID](#stable-id).

### Duplicates

Repeated headings get a number suffix.

#### Example

The first one is `example`.

#### Example

The second one is `example-2`: [first](#example), [second](#example-2).

---

## Bullet lists

`-`, `*` and `+` all work. As in GFM, changing the marker starts a new list, so this is two lists. Without the blank line between them, YAMD adds an info note (Y212) in case the change was a typo:

- Apples
- Bananas

* Carrots
* Leeks

Nesting follows indentation, by any amount:

- Fruit
  - Citrus
      - Lemon
      - Lime
  - Berries
- Vegetables

A list can start right after a paragraph line:
- no blank line needed
- before the first item

## Numbered lists

The list starts at the first number you type; the rest are numbered in order, whatever numbers you type:

1. First
1. Second
1. Third

A code block or quote indented under an item stays in that item, and numbering continues:

1. Clone the repository:

   ```bash
   git clone https://example.com/yamd.git
   ```

2. Install dependencies:

   > Needs Node.js 20 or later.

3. Run the tests.

Only a list starting at 1 can interrupt a paragraph, so a year at the start of a line stays text:
1984. A great year for computing.

To start a new paragraph with a number and a period, escape it: 1984\. A great year.

A list after a blank line can start anywhere:

10. Tenth
11. Eleventh

## Task lists

- [x] Write the spec
- [x] Build the parser
- [ ] Ship the extension
  - [ ] Package the `.vsix`
  - [ ] Write release notes

1. [x] Numbered tasks work too
2. [ ] Like this one

## Rich list items

- **Paragraphs**: an item can hold several paragraphs.

  Indent the next paragraph under the item.

- **Quotes**:
  > A quote inside a list item.

- **Tables**:

  | Key | Value |
  | --- | ----- |
  | a   | 1     |
